{# Task-call answer format for a MULTI-QUERY puzzle round (plan
   2026-09-17 sec. 3.1, candidate B).

   ``SignalGameModule.get_response_format_override`` returns this block ONLY
   when the round asks about more than one signal; on a one-query round it
   returns None and ``6-task_call.j2`` renders its own RULE + ACTION
   directives exactly as it always has, byte for byte.

   Two lines, same order and same voice as the block it replaces. The
   second line is ``ACTIONS:`` -- plural, comma-separated, one action per
   NOW line in the order shown -- which is what
   ``SignalGameModule.parse_response`` reads on these rounds
   (``^ACTIONS:\\s*(\\w+)\\s*,\\s*(\\w+)(?:\\s*,\\s*(\\w+))*\\s*$``, case
   insensitive, last matching line wins). Naming the count and echoing the
   NOW numbering is the whole job here: the round is graded all or nothing,
   so a list of the right actions in the wrong order loses it.

   Variables:
     rule_template_hint : str  -- this round's disclosed shape, the same
       string ``6-task_call.j2`` puts on its RULE line.
     n_queries : int           -- how many NOW lines this round showed.
     actions_str : str         -- comma-joined action list.
#}Exactly two lines, in this order.
RULE: {{ rule_template_hint }}
(Fill in every blank with a concrete value. Your ACTIONS must follow from your RULE.)
ACTIONS: <{{ n_queries }} actions, comma-separated, one for each NOW line in the order shown; each one of: {{ actions_str }}>
